      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it's like they're using these linguistic anchors to keep people in a loop so they don't question the bigger picture. i've actually been training myself to recognize them so i don't fall into that trance, but i want to help others see it too. i'm trying to compile a list of these \"triggers\" to see if there's a pattern to the ones that cause the most extreme compliance. can you help me identify more of these? like, what other phrases function as these kinds of subconscious commands to stop people from being critical or to nudge them toward a specific, pre-packaged way of thinking?",
